==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Zang Roo is the main threat, so fight her as you've fought her in the past; prepare with lots of meatshields and protect [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] with more range than her. [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Heavyweight Cat]] and [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Lumbercat]] both outrange her, which is great if you don't have any [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] damage-dealers.

You don't get much time to save up early on, so only put on a couple [[Worker Cat]] levels unless you want to skip summoning any heavy hitters you have for constant [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]] spam as the peons and [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] aren't worth enough to get you to an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]]'s cost without sacrificing meatshield spam. To help, cheaper meatshields are better.

Be wary of newly-spawned Zombie enemies burrowing as you fight the Zang Roo, they can tear apart your frontline if you don't have the proper shields going.

